# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# retrieval-lab .gitignore
#
# The repository root is the PROJECT root. Three things must never be pushed:
#   1. anything that reveals the answers to the benchmark questions
#   2. the generated fixture corpora and derived search indexes (large, rebuildable)
#   3. virtualenvs and caches
# Everything else - code, tests, findings, reports, plans, run state - is tracked.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- 1. ANSWER KEYS AND MEASUREMENT PRIVACY -------------------------------
# _private/ holds answer_key.json, the canary manifests, and 189 recorded
# measurement sessions. If this leaks, no honest re-run of the benchmark is
# possible. Never remove this rule.
_private/

# The entire fixture tree. harness/generator/ is the machinery that MANUFACTURES
# the answer key - finalize_key.py, canary_slots.py, plant_canaries.py, plan.py -
# and harness/world/ is the ground-truth model every planted answer derives from.
# Publishing either is equivalent to publishing the key, so the whole tree stays
# local. How the fixture was built is described in the reports instead.
harness/

# ACCEPTANCE.md is an oracle in prose: gold source paths, literal cell values
# and page indices for the 30 acceptance cells. Kept local, deliberately.
ACCEPTANCE.md

# Stage 2.2's source audit resolves every frozen question to its gold address.
corpus-lab/state/evidence_v1/

# --- 2. GENERATED CORPORA AND DERIVED INDEXES -----------------------------
# (The four fixture corpora - 15,010 / 5,000 / 2,000 / 500 files - are covered
# by the harness/ rule above. Regeneration is banned anyway: the generator's own
# determinism check failed, so rebuilding would silently change the ground truth.)

# FTS5 page indexes (~7 GB), shelf database, and card vector files.
corpus-lab/02_stacks/s2_fts5/*.db
corpus-lab/02_stacks/s2_fts5/*.db-shm
corpus-lab/02_stacks/s2_fts5/*.db-wal
corpus-lab/02_stacks/s6_hybrid/
corpus-lab/02_stacks/s7_shelf/
corpus-lab/02_stacks/shelf_v2/
corpus-lab/02_stacks/evidence_v1/
corpus-lab/state/shelf_v2/
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
*.npy

# --- 3. ENVIRONMENTS, CACHES, SCRATCH -------------------------------------
.venv/
**/.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/

99_scratch/
99_scratch_test_cwd/
corpus-lab/99_scratch/
*.log
*.bak_pass2

# OS noise
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store

# Holdout question TEXT. The 30-question confirmation set keeps its value
# only while it is unseen; c_queries.json (the dev set) was already published,
# this is not. Kept on disk for resumability, never committed.
corpus-lab/state/c_queries_holdout.json
corpus-lab/state/c_queries_holdout2.json
